            <ArticleTitle>Online 3-dimensional rendering of optical coherence tomography images for the assessment of bifurcation intervention.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>759.e1-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cjca.2012.04.017</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0828-282X(12)00228-0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Three-dimensional optical coherence tomography rendering has been suggested as a method providing additive information for the assessment of the result of percutaneous coronary intervention. However, rendering of such models is very time-consuming and cannot be performed online during the intervention. We present a case in which a new method for 3-dimensional rendering of optical coherence tomography images helped visualize the stent-vessel wall interaction, providing useful information that discouraged further intervention.</AbstractText>
